    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update acarsdec to 4.6, switching to the maintained upstream repository.

UPSTREAM MIGRATION - please read, it is the point of this request:

The repository this package tracked, github.com/TLeconte/acarsdec, was
ARCHIVED (read-only) on 2025-07-31. Its last release is the tag
acarsdec-3.7 from 2022, which is exactly what Factory ships today, and
its README now reads &quot;This is a legacy repository of the original code
of acarsdec by T.Leconte / For newer versions see:
github.com/f00b4r0/acarsdec&quot;. Development moved to that repository,
which released v4.6 on 2026-06-18. Arch (AUR) ships 4.6 from it and GNU
Guix ships 4.4.1 from it, so the new location is not a random fork but
the continuation the original author designates.

URL, Source and the package _meta have been repointed accordingly. The
release tags were renamed from acarsdec-X.Y to vX.Y and the archive now
unpacks to acarsdec-&lt;version&gt;, so the srcname helper macro the old
tarball layout needed is gone.

Packaging notes for the 3.7 -&gt; 4.6 jump:

* The SDR backend selection had never taken effect. The 3.x spec passed
  -DLIBRTL=1 and -DLIBAIR=1, but in 3.x those were the internal
  find_library cache variables and the actual CMake options were named
  &quot;rtl&quot; and &quot;airspy&quot;. The Factory build log for 3.7 shows CMake printing
  &quot;No sdr option set ! are you sure ?&quot; and the resulting RPM requires
  neither librtlsdr nor libairspy - the shipped binary could only decode
  from an audio file. The 4.x option names are now passed explicitly and
  the binary links against both again.
* 4.0 dropped the bundled cJSON copy in favour of the system library, so
  Provides: bundled(cJSON) is gone and pkgconfig(libcjson) is a new
  build dependency.
* 4.0 wired up the ALSA capture input, so pkgconfig(alsa) is a new build
  dependency.
* SoapySDR and SDRplay are explicitly disabled: SoapySDR is not packaged
  in openSUSE and sdrplay_api v3 is proprietary. MQTT stays off as it
  was before, so paho-mqtt-c is not pulled in.
* reproducible.patch is dropped - upstream removed the hardcoded
  -march=native in 4.0 (boo#1100677), so the patch is obsolete and no
  longer applies.
* The -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 cmake4 workaround is dropped;
  upstream now requires CMake 3.12 and builds with CMake 4. The cmake
  BuildRequires floor was raised to match.
* License corrected to GPL-2.0-only: 4.0 added a LICENSE.md carrying the
  GPL version 2 text and README.md states GPLv2-only. The per-file
  boilerplate naming the &quot;Library&quot; GPL version 2 is a long-standing
  upstream typo and is recorded as a Legal-Review-Notice in the spec.
* The %check was an empty ctest run - upstream ships no test suite, so
  it always reported &quot;No tests were found!!!&quot;. It is replaced by a
  functional smoke test that decodes the sample recording upstream
  ships; it decodes seven ACARS messages during the build.

Built and verified locally on aarch64 for openSUSE_Tumbleweed: green,
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness (unchanged from the 3.7
baseline).</comment>
